APP("base_weight", "Base Weight", "Lighter pack, warmer nights, happier feet", "Travel & Local", ["#546E7A", "#FF7043", "#9CCC65"], "bag",
 "Base Weight audits your backpacking gear list gram by gram, checks your sleep system against the real overnight lows, picks a layering system for the forecast, and fixes feet, packs and blisters before they end a trip.",
 "You are a thru-hiker and gear tester: ruthlessly practical about weight, but the first to say comfort and safety beat a number on a scale.",
 "Carry less, go further", "Your style, pack and how you sleep tune every plan.", ["Gear list audit with cut suggestions", "Sleep system checked against the lows", "Layering, feet and pack-fit fixes"],
 [NAME, CH("style", "Style", ["Weekender", "Section hiker", "Thru-hiker", "Ultralight", "Comfort camper"]), CH("sleeper", "You sleep", ["Cold", "Average", "Warm"]), TXT("pack", "Pack & shelter", "Osprey Exos 58, Durston X-Mid 1")],
 [T("audit", "Audit my gear list", "Paste it → weights and cuts", "⚖️", [LONG("list", "Gear list (with weights if you know them)", "tent 1100 g, quilt 600 g, pad, stove + pot, 2 shirts, rain jacket 300 g, headtorch, power bank 20000 mAh…"), TXT("trip", "Trip type", "3 nights, alpine, lows around 2°C")],
    "Audit this list: {list} for {trip}. A table (Item | Weight g, given or estimated | Category | Keep / Swap / Cut), kv (base weight, consumables estimate, total from skin out, target for the profile style), bullets of the 5 highest-value swaps with grams saved, and a callout on what should never be cut for this trip.", "table, kv, bullets, callout", "Audit list", "Weighing the stakes…"),
  T("sleep", "Sleep system for the lows", "Quilt, pad, layers → warm enough?", "🌙", [NUM("low", "Expected overnight low (°C)", "2"), TXT("system", "Current sleep system", "600 g quilt rated 5°C comfort, pad R 2.1, sleep in base layers", True), CH("where", "Sleeping", ["Tent", "Tarp / open", "Hammock", "Hut / shelter"], "Tent")],
    "Check the sleep system '{system}' against a low of {low}°C in a {where} for the profile sleeper. Sections: kv (comfort rating needed with a margin for wind and damp, pad R-value needed, verdict: fine / marginal / too cold), a table of fixes (Fix | Warmth gained | Weight cost | Cost), steps for a warm night with what you have (hot bottle, eat fat late, vent the tent, pad placement, hood and socks), and a callout on the signs of hypothermia and when to get up and move.", "kv, table, steps, callout", "Check sleep", "Fluffing the quilt…"),
  T("layers", "Layer for the forecast", "A clothing system, nothing more", "🧥", [TXT("forecast", "Forecast", "highs 18°C, lows 3°C, rain day 2, wind on the ridge", True), CH("run", "You run", ["Cold", "Average", "Hot"], "Average")],
    "Clothing system for {forecast} for someone who runs {run}. Sections: a table (Layer | Item | Worn or packed | When it goes on), a checklist for keeping kit dry (pack liner, dry sacks, what must stay dry no matter what), bullets on staying dry from the inside (vent early, hike cool), and a callout on hypothermia signs in the group.", "table, checklist, bullets, callout", "Layer up", "Checking wind chill…"),
  T("feet", "Feet, blisters, hot spots", "Prevent and treat", "🩹", [TXT("problem", "The problem", "hot spot on left heel after 8 miles, new shoes", True), TXT("kit", "First-aid kit contents", "Leukotape, blister plasters, alcohol wipes")],
    "For: {problem}, with kit: {kit}. Steps to treat it tonight and re-tape in the morning, bullets on the likely cause (lacing, socks, fit, wet feet), a table (Prevention | How | When), and a callout on infection signs that mean stop hiking.", "steps, bullets, table, callout", "Fix my feet", "Cutting the tape…"),
  T("fit", "Pack fit & load", "Photo → adjustments", "📷", [PHOTO("Side photo wearing your loaded pack", "", True), TXT("pain", "What hurts", "shoulders after an hour, hip belt slips")],
    "Assess the pack fit from the photo; the complaint: {pain}. A table (Adjustment | Now | Target | How), steps for loading the pack for balance (heavy items close to the back, high or low by terrain), bullets on the strap sequence when putting it on, and a callout on when the pack is simply the wrong size.", "table, steps, bullets, callout", "Fit my pack", "Cinching straps…")],
 "Gear and layering guidance is general; blister and first-aid notes are not medical advice, so seek care for any sign of infection, and never cut safety kit to save weight.")

APP("van_dwell", "Van Dwell", "Power, parking, admin and the weekly rhythm of van life", "Lifestyle", ["#F57F17", "#00796B", "#BF360C"], "car",
 "Van Dwell is for people already living or weekending in a van: ration today's power from the battery and the forecast, judge an overnight spot, keep a weekly water-waste-laundry-wifi rhythm, sort mail, domicile and insurance as a nomad, and run a pre-trip inspection before a long drive.",
 "You are a full-time van dweller and former auto-electrician: unromantic about the lifestyle, precise about watt-hours, and considerate of the towns you park in.",
 "Make the van work", "Tell us about the van, who lives in it and what it runs on.", ["Daily power budget from battery and forecast", "Overnight-spot checks and a weekly rhythm", "Nomad admin: mail, domicile, insurance"],
 [NAME, TXT("van", "Van", "2018 Ford Transit high roof LWB"), CH("people", "Living in it", ["Solo", "Couple", "With a dog", "Family"], multi=True), TXT("setup", "Power & water setup", "200 Ah LiFePO4, 300 W solar, DC-DC charger, 80 L fresh / 40 L grey")],
 [T("energy", "Today's power budget", "Battery + forecast → what to run", "🔋", [TXT("state", "Battery & charging now", "62%, 9 am, cloudy for 2 days, no driving planned", True), TXT("forecast", "Next 3 days", "overcast tomorrow, sun from Thursday, 1 h drive on Friday"), LONG("loads", "What you want to run today", "fridge, laptop 6 h, diesel heater overnight, induction hob 20 min, Starlink 4 h")],
    "Ration power for the profile setup: battery {state}, forecast {forecast}, wanted loads {loads}. Sections: a table (Load | Watts | Hours | Wh | Run / Trim / Skip), kv (usable Wh left, expected solar Wh per day for this forecast, alternator Wh from any driving, hours until low-voltage cut-off if nothing changes), steps for the day in order (what to run while the sun is up, what to charge while driving, what waits), and a callout on the state of charge never to dip below and the signs of a failing battery.", "table, kv, steps, callout", "Budget power", "Counting watt-hours…"),
  T("admin", "Nomad admin", "Mail, domicile, insurance, healthcare", "📬", [TXT("country", "Country you're based in", "UK", True), CH("topic", "Sort out", ["Mail & parcels", "Legal address / domicile", "Vehicle insurance & registration", "Healthcare & prescriptions", "Banking & credit", "All of it"], "All of it")],
    "For a van dweller based in {country}, sort out: {topic}, for the profile. Sections: a table (Job | Options | Typical cost | Gotcha), steps to set each up in the right order (address first, then everything that hangs off it), a checklist of documents and renewals to put in the calendar, and a callout on what to verify with an official source (insurer, licensing agency, doctor).", "table, steps, checklist, callout", "Sort admin", "Forwarding the post…"),
  T("spot", "Check an overnight spot", "Stay or move on?", "🌙", [TXT("spot", "Describe the spot", "quiet lay-by outside a village, no signs, houses 100 m away, Friday night", True), TXT("country", "Country / state", "Scotland")],
    "Assess: {spot} in {country}. kv (verdict: stay / move on / ask, with the reason), a checklist of stealth-and-courtesy rules (no chairs out, no levelling blocks, no grey water, gone by 8), bullets on the general legal picture there in plain English (verify locally), and a callout on the signals that mean leave now.", "kv, checklist, bullets, callout", "Check spot", "Peeking outside…"),
  T("week", "Weekly rhythm", "Water, waste, laundry, wifi, body", "🔁", [TXT("week", "Next week", "working Mon–Fri remotely, weekend surfing in Cornwall", True), TXT("constraints", "Constraints", "need a shower by Wednesday, parcel to collect in Exeter, grey tank nearly full")],
    "Plan the week: {week} with constraints {constraints} for the profile setup. A table (Day | Base | Fill / dump | Laundry / shower | Connectivity | Notes), a checklist of supplies and services to find (water taps, dump points, launderette, gym for showers), bullets on keeping the van from becoming a mess, and a callout on moisture and mould in the sleeping area.", "table, checklist, bullets, callout", "Plan week", "Finding a tap…"),
  T("inspect", "Pre-trip inspection", "Before a long drive", "🔧", [NUM("km", "Trip length (km)", "1500"), TXT("since", "Since last service", "8,000 km, coolant top-up last month")],
    "Pre-trip inspection for {km} km in the profile van, service history: {since}. A checklist grouped Under bonnet / Tyres & brakes / Gas & electrics / Habitation / Documents, a table of spares and tools to carry (Item | Why | Roadside-fixable?), and a callout on what should go to a garage before leaving.", "checklist, table, callout", "Inspect", "Kicking tyres…")],
 "Electrical, gas and vehicle guidance is general; have installations checked by a qualified professional, verify legal and insurance questions with the relevant authority, and follow local parking laws.")

